<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancho Garcés I of Pamplona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 925</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancho Garcés I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> from 905 to 925 and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimenez-dynasty">Jiménez dynasty</a>. He displaced the Íñiguez line, expanded his kingdom south into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rioja">La Rioja</a>, and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-qasi">Banu Qasi</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. Though defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> at Valdejunquera in 920, he established Pamplona, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, as a leading Christian kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sancho-garces-i-of-pamplona.jpg" alt="Sancho Garcés I of Pamplona" width="295" height="568" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sancho_I_Abarca_de_Navarra_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
